content"><p>Given two integer arrays <code>preorder</code> and <code>inorde=
r</code> where <code>preorder</code> is the preorder traversal of a binary =
tree and <code>inorder</code> is the inorder traversal of the same tree, co=
nstruct and return <em>the binary tree</em>.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>
<img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/02/19/tree.jp=
g" style=3D"width: 277px; height: 302px;">
<pre><strong>Input:</strong> preorder =3D [3,9,20,15,7], inorder =3D [9,3,1=
5,20,7]
<strong>Output:</strong> [3,9,20,null,null,15,7]
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> preorder =3D [-1], inorder =3D [-1]
<strong>Output:</strong> [-1]
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D preorder.length &lt;=3D 3000</code></li>
	<li><code>inorder.length =3D=3D preorder.length</code></li>
	<li><code>-3000 &lt;=3D preorder[i], inorder[i] &lt;=3D 3000</code></li>
	<li><code>preorder</code> and <code>inorder</code> consist of <strong>uniq=
ue</strong> values.</li>
	<li>Each value of <code>inorder</code> also appears in <code>preorder</cod=
e>.</li>
	<li><code>preorder</code> is <strong>guaranteed</strong> to be the preorde=
r traversal of the tree.</li>
	<li><code>inorder</code> is <strong>guaranteed</strong> to be the inorder =
traversal of the tree.</li>
</ul>
